      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-05T10:05:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I think the series is a year or so ahead of real time anyway, because of the year that was skipped between \"The End of the World\" and \"Aliens in London\", when the Doctor then brings Rose home and tells her it's only been twelve hours, when in fact it's been twelve months. I would not bne remotely surprised to discover that there's a website or two out there with a very specific timeline (or at least, as specific as possible) laying out all the events that have taken place in the new series so far.</p>",
